@@ -0,0 +1,179 @@
+# Low-pass filtering in OAR rendering paths
+
+This document catalogs every rendering path in OAR that applies a low-pass
+filter, describes each filter's design and configuration, and — equally
+important — lists the paths that carry LFE content but apply **no** filtering,
+since that is a common source of confusion.
+
+OAR contains exactly two low-pass filters:
+
+| # | Filter | Location | Cutoff | When it runs |
+|---|--------|----------|--------|--------------|
+| 1 | LFE synthesis biquad (EAR, HOA→loudspeakers) | `src/renderer/ear/h2m_rdr.c` | 120 Hz | Per audio block, only when rendering a scene-based (HOA) element to an LFE-bearing loudspeaker layout, and only if built with `OAR_ENABLE_HOA_LFE` |
+| 2 | Windowed-sinc anti-aliasing filter (OBR resampler) | `src/renderer/obr/obr_capi/obr/obr/ambisonic_binaural_decoder/resampler.cc` | Nyquist of the lower rate | At binaural renderer initialization, while resampling HRIR assets to the stream sample rate |
+
+Everything else — channel-bed downmixing, object panning, and binaural LFE
+handling — is pure gain routing with no spectral shaping.
+
+---
+
+## 1. EAR HOA→loudspeakers (H2M): 120 Hz LFE synthesis filter
+
+When a scene-based (Ambisonics) audio element is rendered to a loudspeaker
+layout that contains LFE channels, the EAR renderer *synthesizes* the LFE
+signal, since HOA has no LFE channel of its own. The LFE feed is derived from
+the W (omni) channel and low-pass filtered at 120 Hz.
+
+### Build gating
+
+The path is compiled out by default:
+
+- `ae_rdr.h:91-92` defaults `DISABLE_LFE_HOA` to `1` (LFE channels are written
+  as silence).
+- The CMake option `OAR_ENABLE_HOA_LFE` (`CMakeLists.txt:36-39`) defines
+  `DISABLE_LFE_HOA=0`, enabling LFE generation and the filter.
+
+With the feature disabled, `IAMF_element_renderer_render_H2M` still reserves
+the LFE channel slots in the output layout but zero-fills them
+(`h2m_rdr.c:2408-2421`).
+
+### Filter design
+
+`lfe_filter_t` (`ae_rdr.h:95-99`) holds the coefficients and two samples of
+input/output history. `lfefilter_init` (`h2m_rdr.c:2465`) computes a
+second-order IIR (biquad) low-pass via the bilinear transform:
+
+```
+c  = 1 / tan(pi * fc / fs)
+a1 = 1 / (1 + c + c^2)        b1 = 2 * (1 - c^2) * a1
+a2 = 2 * a1                   b2 = (1 - c + c^2) * a1
+a3 = a1
+```
+
+`lfefilter_update` (`h2m_rdr.c:2486`) runs the direct-form difference
+equation per sample. A `cutoff_freq <= 0` zeroes all coefficients (the filter
+outputs silence) rather than dividing by zero.
+
+### Initialization and the sample-rate contract
+
+The filter must be designed for the *actual* stream rate, not an assumed one:
+
+- Eager init: `ear.c:276-279` — when the H2M matrix is fetched and the output
+  layout has an LFE1 channel, `lfefilter_init(plfe, 120, ctx->sample_rate)`
+  is called once (guarded by `plfe->init`).
+- Lazy fallback: `lfefilter_update` (`h2m_rdr.c:2490-2495`) initializes an
+  untouched filter at 120 Hz using the `sample_rate` argument threaded through
+  `IAMF_element_renderer_render_H2M`.
+
+Historically the fallback hardcoded 48 kHz, which scaled the effective cutoff
+with the output rate (~240 Hz at 96 kHz). Fixed in commit `c772ef2` (#15);
+`tests/examples/test_hoa_lfe_rendering.c` is the regression test asserting the
+LFE level for a given tone is invariant to the output sampling rate.
+
+### Signal flow per block
+
+`IAMF_element_renderer_render_H2M` (`h2m_rdr.c:2367`):
+
+1. The HOA input is matrix-rendered to the non-LFE loudspeaker channels using
+   a predefined matrix from `h2m_rdr_tab` (selected by
+   `IAMF_element_renderer_get_H2M_matrix`, keyed on HOA order × output sound
+   system). The matrix rows exclude LFE; `h2m_rdr_t.lfe1`/`.lfe2`
+   (`ae_rdr.h:146-147`) give the LFE channel indices in the output layout, or
+   `-1` if absent.
+2. Rendered channels are shifted to make room at the LFE index positions
+   (`h2m_rdr.c:2386-2406`).
+3. For each sample, the LFE signal is the filtered W channel (`in[0]`),
+   scaled for the layout size (`h2m_rdr.c:2425-2438`):
+   - `output * 0.5` when the layout has ≤ 2 channels,
+   - `output / sqrt(n)` otherwise, where `n` is the output channel count.
+4. If the layout has a second LFE channel (LFE2), it receives a copy of the
+   LFE1 signal; when only LFE2 exists it is computed the same way
+   (`h2m_rdr.c:2440-2457`). There is a single filter state per renderer
+   (`IAMF_SP_LAYOUT.lfe_f`, `ae_rdr.h:118`), so both LFE channels carry the
+   same signal.
+
+Passing a NULL `lfe_filter_t *` disables synthesis at runtime and writes
+silence to the LFE channels.
+
+## 2. OBR binaural path: resampler windowed-sinc low-pass
+
+The binaural renderer (built with `OAR_ENABLE_BINAURALIZER`) embeds a
+polyphase resampler whose interpolation filter is a low-pass. It is **not**
+part of the per-block audio path — OBR processes audio at the stream rate —
+it runs once at initialization to resample the built-in spherical-harmonic
+HRIR assets to the stream's sample rate.
+
+### Where it runs
+
+- `ObrImpl` owns one shared `Resampler` (`obr_impl.h:249-252`) and passes it
+  to each processing group (`obr_impl.cc:105`, `processing_group.cc:57`).
+- `sh_hrir_creator.cc:35-60` (`CreateShHrirsFromWav`) compares the HRIR WAV
+  rate to the target stream rate and, if they differ, calls
+  `Resampler::SetRateAndNumChannels(wav_rate, target_rate, ...)` followed by
+  `Resampler::Process` over the HRIR channels.
+
+### Filter design
+
+`Resampler::GenerateInterpolatingFilter` (`resampler.cc:263-286`):
+
+- Cutoff: `sample_rate / (2 * max(up_rate, down_rate))` — the Nyquist
+  frequency of the lower of the two rates, giving anti-aliasing on
+  downsampling and anti-imaging on upsampling.
+- Kernel: Hann-windowed sinc (`GenerateSincFilter`, `resampler.cc:310-338`),
+  length `max_rate * kTransitionBandwidthRatio` with
+  `kTransitionBandwidthRatio = 13` (`resampler.cc:36-40`), normalized so the
+  polyphase branches sum to unity gain times `up_rate`.
+- The kernel is decomposed into `up_rate` polyphase branches
+  (`ArrangeFilterAsPolyphase`). The per-branch length is derived from
+  `up_rate`; deriving it from `max_rate` previously truncated the kernel tail
+  when downsampling, causing rate-dependent gain loss and degraded
+  anti-aliasing — fixed in commit `b8ceea9` (#14).
+
+## 3. Paths that carry LFE but apply NO low-pass filter
+
+These paths route or synthesize bass content by gain only. If bass management
+or LFE band-limiting is expected there, it must be applied downstream.
+
+### EAR multichannel→multichannel (M2M)
+
+`m2m_rdr.c` renders channel beds through static downmix gain matrices
+(predefined layouts via `IAMF_element_renderer_render_M2M`, custom layouts via
+the `_custom` variant). LFE input channels map to LFE output channels with
+unit gain (see e.g. the LFE rows at `m2m_rdr.c:154`, `:172`); no filtering is
+performed anywhere in this path.
+
+### Downmix renderer
+
+`src/renderer/downmix/downmix_renderer.c` implements the IAMF demixing-based
+downmix. It is pure gain/matrix arithmetic; the LFE channel passes through
+untouched.
+
+### OLR object renderer
+
+The object (OLR) panner never routes objects into LFE channels: gain
+calculation runs on a layout with LFE speakers removed
+(`custom_gain_calculator.c:264`, `speaker_layout_wo_lfe`). There is no filter
+in the OLR tree.
+
+### OBR binaural rendering of LFE channels
+
+When channel beds (or the `ck_ri_id_lfe` / `ck_ri_id_lfe_pair` subsets,
+mapped in `obr.c:60,72`) are binauralized, LFE channels are treated as
+ordinary virtual loudspeakers:
+
+- `loudspeaker_layouts.h:154-159` positions them at azimuth 0°, elevation
+  −30° (`kLFE`), and ±45°, −30° (`kLFE1`/`kLFE2`), with the `is_LFE` flag set.
+- The `is_LFE` flag is informational only: its sole consumer is the debug
+  table formatter (`audio_element_table_formatter.cc:185`). No renderer
+  component branches on it, so LFE content is HRTF-convolved full-band like
+  any other channel — no 120 Hz filter, no bass management.
+
+## Summary
+
+| Path | Renderer | LFE / bass handling | Low-pass? |
+|------|----------|--------------------|-----------|
+| HOA → loudspeakers | EAR (`h2m_rdr.c`) | LFE synthesized from W channel | Yes — 120 Hz biquad (needs `OAR_ENABLE_HOA_LFE`) |
+| Channels → loudspeakers | EAR (`m2m_rdr.c`) | Matrix gain routing | No |
+| Channels → channels (demix) | Downmix (`downmix_renderer.c`) | Gain routing | No |
+| Objects → loudspeakers | OLR | LFE excluded from panning | No |
+| Anything → binaural | OBR | LFE binauralized as a positioned channel | No (audio path); sinc LPF only inside HRIR resampling at init |
