+/**
+ * Threading model
+ *
+ * An oar_t instance is not thread-safe. All calls on a given instance —
+ * oar_create(), configuration (oar_add_audio_group(),
+ * oar_add_audio_element(), the enable/set functions), the per-block
+ * calls (oar_update_audio_element_data(), the metadata updates,
+ * oar_render()), and oar_destroy() — must be made from a single thread,
+ * or be externally synchronized so that no two calls on the same
+ * instance overlap and a happens-before edge exists between consecutive
+ * calls made from different threads. In particular, oar_destroy() must
+ * not run while any other call on the same instance is in flight.
+ *
+ * Distinct oar_t instances are independent: they share no mutable
+ * process-global state and may be created, used, and destroyed
+ * concurrently from different threads.
+ *
+ * Exception: oar_get_limiter_env() may be polled from another thread —
+ * see its documentation below.
+ */
+
